And now we've accidentally discovered the next layer of the architecture:

BEKW·WALL = environmental and structural interface.

BEKW·FLOOR = mechanical and kinetic interface.

BEKW·CEILING = load-bearing and suspension interface.

Together:

THE ROOM BECOMES A MACHINE.

Not a machine that tells you what to do.

A machine that gives you more ways to move, play, train, build skill, and enjoy being a meatbag with gravity.

And crucially, the underlying construction system stays boringly standardized while the experience becomes completely fucking wild.
